            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kirsten Finnigan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was an excellent family or casual, dinner-for-friends recipe. It gave the tender pork chops a delicate bbq flavor. I used the thick boneless chops from Sam's Club (9 of them), seared them on my non-stick grill pan and doubled the sauce recipe to bake. Got rave reviews all around the table. The chops cut easily with a fork. So simple, yet so good.",
            "datePublished": "2004-03-31T12:23:20.217Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tam76"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As this recipe is written, I think it would have been very bland, but I made some changes as suggested by other reviews. I added the onion and garlic, and I used bottled bbq sauce instead of ketchup. I did them in the slow cooker, so they were nice and moist. The whole family enjoyed them!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-10T10:53:20.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Melissa Young"
            },
            "reviewBody": "loved it after the changes I made. I marinated them for one hour in sauce. instead of ketchup I used honey bbq sauce and I used no salt, celery seed, or bay leaf. instead of nutmeg I used truffle powder, instead of the vinegar I used lemon juice. and of course I used water and onions. I didn't really measure anything just added to taste. and I used the same cooking time and temperature.",
            "datePublished": "2018-05-03T12:30:18.533Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Veronica Corza"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this recipe. Marinate overnight, even better! I used less vinegar about 1/4 cup and crushed the bay leaf.",
            "datePublished": "2010-03-04T09:53:38.990Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PANITO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very easy, very tasty recipe. I made only a couple of changes. First do not cook for 90 minutes. I let it cook for an hour and I still think that was too long. Second I did away completely with the ketchup and added bottled bbq sauce instead. I also added some garlic powder. This is a good recipe and easy to adjust to your taste. Remember to baste frequently. I will make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2005-01-24T10:24:55.670Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Arthurs"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were good. I did not brown and only cooked for 30-45 minutes. I added fresh garlic and onions and thickened the sauce. Nxt time I will try these in the crockpot.",
            "datePublished": "2007-02-21T17:31:04.183Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Annie Lee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used apple cider vinegar, added brown sugar, and chopped onion. I omitted nutmeg and cooked them to 145 degrees. Yummy.",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-11T22:43:09.587Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "David Smith"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Chops were nice and tender. The sauce was pretty good. I made it with rice wine vinegar and added some crushed red pepper flakes.",
            "datePublished": "2019-03-25T13:31:40.387Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mandieh24"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought this was pretty good. My hubby and I both agreed on a 4 star rating. I did make some small modifications. I used 1/2 C. aplle cider vinegar and the rest as white vinegar. I also added in a few ybsp. of bottled bbq at the advice of the other readers. I added some gar;ic and onion powder and a tbsp. of splenda to sweeten it up. I baked the chops in the oven for 30 minutes and pulled them out and thickened the sauce with some flour because the sauce was pretty runny. I used really thin chops, so they were a little more dry than I would have liked. All in all, I will make this again. Thanks for sharing :D",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-15T19:11:30.413Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Songer Willard Frye"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good. Tastey, texture was good from baking at a low temp for longer than usual, and blended very well with (I know this sounds weird) French Fries. I have longterm Covid and my taste is off the norm, so when things taste good to me, it's definitely a plus. Will be making again.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-30T02:00:32.009Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Gardner Wilbur"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the same recipe that my Mother used to make. I prepared it for several who had never had it and they raved about it. It shouldn't be dry unless you let the sauce thicken too much. Add more water every now and then if this happens while cooking. Also I use a round roasting pan with a lid. It is better if you leave the lid on for an hour then off for the last thirty minutes. I doubled the recipe and it was wonderful!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-11-26T14:49:31.703Z"
          },
          {
